  "title": "The end of the price-on-the-windshield era",
  "summary": "The FTC’s March 2026 warning letters to 97 auto dealership groups marked a turning point: the agency is enforcing total-price disclosure case by case, and OEMs in powersports, marine, RV and LSV are already advising dealers to revisit how they advertise. This piece breaks down where dealers actually get exposed, why the same patterns extend across every titled-vehicle segment, and how disclosure-by-design turns compliance into a byproduct of a cleaner buyer experience.",
